# React Flow viewer (browser demo)

Canonical decisions: sibling monorepo
`executioncontrolprotocol/packages/extensions/format-reactflow/REACTFLOW_RENDER.md`
(or local copy under that package path).

## Must follow

- Render only `ecp-step` nodes; ignore group wrappers if present in JSON.
- Draw only data edges with both `sourceHandle` and `targetHandle`.
- Every schema port gets a handle: hollow if unconnected, solid if connected.
- Idle routes: solid cyan matching input handles (`--color-tertiary-fixed-dim`).
- During run: marching ants on in-flight edges; green when source step completed.
- Node pulse: soft, low-spread shadow on **running** only; keep a clear green completed glow.
- Do not open the state modal on Run click — open when the run finishes; keep **Inspect state** in the zoom/fit Controls.
- Configure dialog: removable literals after save, add unbound Zod params, editable `as` with ref rewrite; save via `ecp.patch` + `syncFromManifest`.
- Canvas connect: output→input writes `$ref` into target `step.input` (Fluent `ref(...)`); delete edge removes that key; same patch + sync path. Do not treat RF edges as source of truth—re-encode after patch. Source must have `as`; replace literal silently on connect.
- Connect type compatibility (demo-local): match `portTypeKind` from `valueSchema`/`typeLabel` (`number`≡`integer`; `unknown` pairs with anything). During output drag, grey + cross incompatible inputs (`ecp-rf-port--incompatible` / `ecp-rf-handle--incompatible`); `isValidConnection` + `isConnectable` reject them.
- Map editors from port **`valueSchema`** (demo-local); fall back to `typeLabel`. Never put widget names in the encode document.
  - short `string` → text input; long (`prompt`/`system`/… or length/`\n`) → textarea
  - `object`/`array`/unknown → Monaco JSON; `number` → number input; `boolean` → toggle
  - `string`+`enum` ≤4 → radios; >4 → `<select>`; `array`+`items.enum` → checkbox multi-select
